<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kushite Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kingdom of Kush, Kushite kingdom, Kushites, Kushite</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kushite Empire, or Kingdom of Kush, was a Nubian state on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, centred successively on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerma">Kerma</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napata">Napata</a> and Meroe. Long under Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> rule, Kush later conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and ruled it as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twenty-fifth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twenty-Fifth Dynasty</a> in the eighth and seventh centuries BCE. Its later Meroitic phase declined in the fourth century CE, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a> rose to the south-east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kushite-empire.jpg" alt="Kushite Empire" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthias Gehricke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rulers_of_Kush,_Kerma_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
